From 066db198eb2edb357d92cc1b8dc5cbfdfcefba18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Netflate <netflate@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:36:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bug 2087615 - [Wayland] Align wl_shm pool size to page size
 and stride to 256 bytes r=stransky,gtk-reviewers

Compositors that support importing wl_shm pools to GPU memory via
udmabuf (which avoids a copy) need the pool to be a whole number of
pages. For udmabuf to work and show a correct image on all drivers,
the stride is also aligned to 256 bytes and stored in
BufferSurface::mStrides[0], so all code accessing SHM buffer memory
uses it instead of width * bpp.

Some drivers don't reject a udmabuf import with an unaligned stride
but silently show a broken image instead (Bug 2088923).

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340639

Adapted for 161: the gfx/layers/NativeLayerWaylandSurfaceHandler.cpp hunk is
dropped, that file does not exist on this branch (it was added by the
NativeLayerWayland refactor in bug 2064944 after 161 branched).

Origin: https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/commit/066db198eb2edb357d92cc1b8dc5cbfdfcefba18
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-23
